extends RefCounted

const TOPICS := [
	["Abyssal Plant · Swimming", "Act II has a flooded service conduit before Pressure Breach. Move to swim horizontally. Hold Jump or Up to rise; hold Down or Crouch to dive. Releasing movement slows you to a gentle upward drift. Dash gives a brief underwater burst. Your blaster, suits, melee and quick-use supplies still work underwater.", "Dive underneath the first hanging bulkhead, then rise over the second barrier. The exit has a dry landing and a shared squad checkpoint. There is no oxygen timer. Water movement uses solid collisions and the same simulation for the host and joining players."],
	["Abyssal Plant · Pressure Breach", "Blue water columns lift you at a capped speed; you can steer out and dash toward a landing. Electrical grids charge amber before the blue discharge. Wait for the discharge to fade, or stand on an amber-edged ceramic refuge: its insulation protects you while your feet stay planted. Turbine blades rotate through the lane; watch the openings before jumping.", "Act II: hold Interact beside each of three red pressure valves. Releasing early cancels the hold. Valve A also reverses the upper current toward a harder cache route. Pressure takes 90 active gameplay seconds to bleed away. Once all three valves are open and pressure reaches zero, the release lock stays open for the entire party. Valves and the open lock survive saving and co-op reconnection. The current-fed maintenance chimney rewards controlled wall kicks with a cache. Each act still requires both Gate Relays to open its boss door."],
	["Frozen Reactor · Rocket Spillway", "In Act II, hold Up by the board at the midpoint checkpoint. Press Jump to hop the short gaps or clear floor spikes. Boost pads launch the board across the long breaks. Hold Jump to glide and release it to drop into a landing sooner. The board cannot jump again in midair.", "Crouch under every overhead spike gate and brake Left to make room for a jump. Watch the warning and distance at the top of the HUD. You can fire your Buster at spillway patrols. The course is 2,460 metres, takes at least two minutes, and activates Gate Relay A for the squad when a rider reaches the exit."],
	["Machine Jungle · Vine Crossing", "Hold Up as you reach a vine. Let it swing forward, then press Jump and steer toward the next grab or landing. There is no floor under the crossing.", "In Act II, use the high vine first, then land on the lower leaf so you can line up the last jump. Follow that route to one Gate Relay. Take the ferry route to find the other."],
	["Deployment", "Choose a sector and difficulty at Deploy. In each act, activate both Gate Relays to open the boss room. Beat the miniboss in Act I and take the Act II gate. Defeat the guardian in Act II, then open the boss cache and extract to bank your rewards.", "Clear a sector on Normal to unlock Hard there and improve your odds of rare loot. Clear every sector on Hard to unlock Expert. In co-op, every operator needs the difficulty unlocked. The NOVA Archive shows a sector's loot after your first clear."],
	["Movement & traversal", "Hold jump for more height. Use an air dash near the top of the jump to cross long gaps. Hold toward a wall while airborne to slide down it, then jump off and steer back to climb. Press up as you reach ladders or vines to grab them.", "On a drop-through deck, hold crouch and press Dash (B on the default Xbox layout). RX-07 stays crouched under low ceilings until there's room to stand. Brake early on frosted decking. Check the binding pages in Settings for your controls."],
	["Buster, saber & suits", "Tap Buster for one shot. In the Standard Frame, hold and release Buster to pierce raised purple shields. Tap Sword in rhythm for a combo or hold and release in the Standard Frame for a ranged slice.", "Defeating a guardian unlocks its suit for the current run. Cycle suits with the shoulder buttons or your swap controls. Press Suit Weapon to spend energy on the equipped suit's attack. Regular Buster shots are available in every suit."],
	["Checkpoints & reconstruction", "Touch a checkpoint to set your return point. A death uses a life. Your HUD includes any bonus lives you banked from challenges. Run out of lives and NOVA reconstructs you at the station. You can deploy to any previously unlocked sector.", "Reconstruction resets your Operator Level and run suits and clears your equipped gear and quick slots. Your Player Level, stored items, banked currency, learned recipes and permanent enhancements carry over."],
	["Shop & currency", "Spend Bolts in the Workshop’s Buy tab on recovery supplies, buffs and crafting materials. Your Operator Level unlocks better stock. To stow purchases, open Operator → Storage and select an Inventory stack, then choose Stow Stack.", "Boss clears and challenges reward Core Shards. Spend them on permanent talents in Core Ascension, in the Workshop."],
	["Core Ascension", "Spend Core Shards in Survivability, Damage or Scavenger. Install one talent in each earlier tier to advance in that branch. Every talent has three ranks. Tier 5 introduces a capstone at Player Level 28 that can reach Rank III at Player Level 50.", "Every co-op player can revive a fallen teammate. Stand beside their body and hold Field Interact for four seconds until the progress bar fills. Releasing the button, moving away or taking damage interrupts the revive. They return at full HP without gaining spare lives. Field Reboot reduces the hold time to 3.2, 2.6 or 2 seconds. Bodies lost to a fall return to their last safe platform. One teammate reaching a checkpoint saves it for the whole squad."],
	["Foundry routes", "The Kiln Warden awards one run module of your choice. In Act II, step on the lower gallery's pressure plate to release the return shutter, and break the cracked wall to open the route. The rolling slag boulder takes ten regular Buster hits or four charged hits. Shoot it from outside the chute.", "The upper gantry and low cooling tunnel have different loot. When the escape warning flashes, climb across the shaft before the lava reaches you. On Expert, shoot the lit relief valve after the Forge Titan's rupture charge to vent the flames and expose his core."],
	["Blueprint hunts", "After your first clear, visit the NOVA Archive and pin a blueprint from that sector's boss cache. Deploy shows the source, minimum difficulty, required Operator Level and progress.", "Three eligible extractions earn the pinned blueprint if it hasn't dropped. Your hunt progress stays with the operator when saved."],
	["Equipment & Storage", "In Gear, choose a socket to see compatible items. Equip one item per socket and check the operator's stats. In Storage, select a stack on the left to move it to the right.", "Salvage recovered in a mission goes to Storage when you extract. Equipped gear stays at risk on a run."],
	["Quick slots", "Assign a supply to a D-pad direction from Equipment or the mission pause inventory. Each direction holds one item type, up to three of that item. The upper limit for an inventory stack is 100.", "Press the assigned direction during gameplay to use one supply. Health and energy supplies only consume when there is something to restore. Recovery items and temporary buffs are described on their item cards."],
	["Blueprints & Crafting", "Select a blueprint in Storage, choose Learn Blueprint, and confirm Unlock Recipe. In the Workshop, review the cost and choose Craft & Equip or Craft to Storage. Equipping sends the old gear to Storage.", "Boss caches guarantee a blueprint and can also contain materials and supplies."],
	["Social & co-op", "Use Social to add friends and accept invites. Open the party screen to create or join a group. The leader picks the sector and starts the mission. Press Enter in the station or in the field to chat with the whole party or reply to a whisper.", "Teammate health appears beneath your own HUD. Loot, lives and inventories are personal. The party shares kill XP and boss suit unlocks. Everyone still in the fight needs to cross the boss door before it closes."],
	["Operator and Profile XP", "Defeating enemies and bosses earns Operator XP. Leveling up raises your stats and restores half of your new maximum HP, up to full health. NOVA resets Operator Level when reconstructing you after a failed run.", "Extract from both acts of a sector to earn permanent Player Profile XP. Visit Profile for your career stats, cosmetics and account settings."],
	["Voice chat", "Open Settings → Audio to enable party voice and select your input and output devices. Use Test Microphone to watch the input meter and hear yourself live through the selected output.", "Bind Push to Talk under Keyboard & Mouse or Controller. The mic beside a party member lights up while their voice is coming through."],
	["Challenges", "Each unlocked sector has five challenges. Requirements can include reaching Act II, extracting at high health, moving quickly or gathering salvage.", "Claim earned rewards from the Challenges tab at the station. New tasks appear at local midnight, and earned rewards remain available after reset."],
	["System & Save", "Use the System pad to save your operator manually. Manage your three slots from the title screen or the Operator station's Operators tab. A save includes banked progress and the current deployment when available.", "Settings covers audio, video, gameplay, keyboard and controller bindings, and installed game updates. Toggle first-time hub tips in Gameplay. This manual remains available either way."],
]
